<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Umnin [Laws of Craftsmen]<br>Halacha 4</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Umnin &mdash; Halacha 4: Part B (&sect;&sect;8&ndash;12)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;8</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Rosh HaShanah</span>. For on Rosh HaShanah, Adam HaRishon was created &mdash; he who must complete the entire creation that was created for his sake, as above, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;which G&ndash;d created to make&rdquo;</span> [asher bara Elokim la&rsquo;asos]. That the entire creation that Hashem, blessed be He, created &mdash; He created everything &ldquo;to make&rdquo; &mdash; that man should need to make and repair and complete all things, for the wheat needs to be ground, etc., as above. And the essential completeness and repair of all the labors and the craftsmanship is through emunah, which is the completeness of all things. And this is what is needed on Rosh HaShanah &mdash; on which Adam HaRishon was created for this purpose, as above.</p>

<p>Therefore the entire avodah [service] of Rosh HaShanah is to draw emunah into the world &mdash; through which is the essential revelation of His sovereignty, blessed be He, which is what we engage in on Rosh HaShanah. As we say many times: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And may You alone, Hashem, reign&rdquo;</span> [v&rsquo;simloch Atah Hashem l&rsquo;vadecha], etc., &ldquo;reign over the entire world in its entirety,&rdquo; etc. And we conclude all the blessings with &ldquo;King over all the earth,&rdquo; etc. For the essential purpose of Rosh HaShanah is to reveal His sovereignty, blessed be He, which is the aspect of emunah, as is known. For it is impossible to accept His sovereignty, blessed be He, except through emunah. And through this one completes the entire creation, whose essential completeness is through man, who was created on this day, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore we say on Rosh HaShanah: &ldquo;This is the day, the beginning of Your works&rdquo; [zeh hayom t&rsquo;chilas ma&rsquo;asecha] &mdash; even though the majority of creation was created in the first five days, from the twenty-fifth of Elul until Rosh HaShanah, as our Sages of blessed memory said. However, since on Rosh HaShanah man was created &mdash; for whose sake everything was created, and he repairs and completes everything &mdash; therefore it is considered as if the entire creation was created on this day. And therefore our Sages of blessed memory said: &ldquo;In Tishrai the world was created&rdquo; &mdash; because on it man was created, and he is the essential one (as is brought regarding this), for he completes everything, as above.</p>

<p>And the essential emunah is impossible to receive except through the tzadikay hador [the righteous of the generation] who are the true guardians of the bris [covenant]. For emunah depends on the bris (as is explained in siman 31 mentioned above). Therefore one must travel to the true tzadikim on Rosh HaShanah &mdash; in order to merit through them complete emunah, which is the essential purpose of Rosh HaShanah, as above. For the tzaddik is the one who guards the bris [tzaddik hu ma&rsquo;an d&rsquo;natir bris].</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;9</div>

<p>And behold, it is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above that through tikun habris [repair of the covenant] one merits to make n&rsquo;fashos [souls], etc. For one merits ahavah [love] and <span class="key-term">kisufin d&rsquo;k&rsquo;dushah</span> [holy yearnings] that are very precious. Through this one makes n&rsquo;fashos, which are the aspect of n&rsquo;kudos [vowel points] for the letters of the Torah &mdash; through which is the essential combining and pairing of the letters of the Torah to perform some action. And see there, all of this explained well. And see what is printed nearby in the passage beginning &ldquo;The combining and joining of the letters,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; see there.</p>

<p>And this is: <span class="verse">&ldquo;There is a hevel [breath/vanity] that is done on the earth&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Koheles 8:14)</span>, etc. And this is the aspect of the gilgulai han&rsquo;fashos [reincarnations of souls], etc. And the general principle is that the yearnings and the longing for something holy are very precious, for through them the nefesh [soul] comes into being and is completed through speech, and goes out and rolls about. And sometimes the holy nefesh rolls and comes into the wicked person, and thoughts of teshuvah [repentance] fall upon him, and he can be brought back to good. And likewise the reverse, etc.</p>

<p>And this is: &ldquo;There is a hevel,&rdquo; etc. Hevel is the breath of the mouth [hevel peh], from which the souls emerge. And through this, there are tzadikim, etc., and there are wicked people to whom it reaches like the deeds of the tzadikim &mdash; through a holy breath rolling into them, that is, a nefesh from good yearnings, etc.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;10</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">shofar</span> of Rosh HaShanah. For the breaths [havalim] of the shofar are the aspect of holy breaths, the aspect of holy souls &mdash; through which the wicked return in teshuvah, as above. And this is what is needed on Rosh HaShanah, which is the first day of the Ten Days of Teshuvah. And all of this we receive from the true tzadikim, to whom we travel and to whom we bind ourselves. For they are the aspect of &ldquo;masters of the soul&rdquo; [ba&rsquo;alay nefesh], from whom are drawn all the souls and the holy breaths &mdash; through which one can bring all the wicked back in teshuvah.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the shofar of a ram [ayil], which is the ram of Yitzchak who was bound upon the altar &mdash; in order that the merit of his binding should be remembered for us. That is, the essential merit of the Akeidah [binding] of Yitzchak is the aspect of ratzon [will] and holy yearnings [kisufin d&rsquo;k&rsquo;dushah]. For this was the essential greatness of the nisayon [test] of Avraham and Yitzchak &mdash; the essential merit was that they were willing to slaughter and to die for the sanctification of Hashem. And through being willing for this with a complete and true will, it was considered as if he had actually been slaughtered and offered upon the altar &mdash; even though in truth He did not send forth His hand against him and did not do anything to him. It emerges that the essential merit of the Akeidah is only ratzon and holy yearnings.</p>

<p>And because Yitzchak merited such holy yearnings in truth, with such self-sacrifice &mdash; from there is drawn the holiness of the souls of Israel who came forth from him. For in each and every one of Israel there is a holy soul that is willing to sacrifice itself for the sanctification of Hashem always. It emerges that every one of Israel &mdash; his soul and his will are strong always for Hashem, blessed be He. For every one of Israel is prepared to die for the sanctification of Hashem, for in the innermost depths of his soul his will is very, very strong for Hashem, blessed be He. And this is because we are all children of Yitzchak our father, who was bound upon the altar and wanted to die for His sake, blessed be He.</p>

<p>And the innermost depths of this breath and this will &mdash; this is what we draw into the shofar, which is the aspect of the shofar of the ram of Yitzchak. For then, at the time of the Akeidah, the ram was sanctified in his place, and then its horn was sanctified as a shofar &mdash; so that Israel, the seed of Yitzchak, should merit to draw the innermost depths of the holy breaths and souls that are rooted in them from Yitzchak. They draw them and bring them out through the holy shofar, which encompasses all the breaths and voices, as it is brought in the holy Zohar: &ldquo;The place from which all voices go forth is called shofar.&rdquo; And through bringing forth the innermost depths of the soul &mdash; which are the aspect of holy breaths &mdash; from within the shofar, through this everyone returns in teshuvah. For these holy breaths are the aspect of holy souls that have the power to go and roll about and bring the entire world back in teshuvah &mdash; and this is what is needed on Rosh HaShanah. And as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above, the great power of the holy breaths to bring the wicked back in teshuvah, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;11</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="key-term">t&rsquo;kiah, sh&rsquo;varim, t&rsquo;ruah, t&rsquo;kiah</span>.</p>

<p><em>T&rsquo;kiah</em> is the aspect of the striking of a hand [t&rsquo;kias kaf] &mdash; the aspect of binding oneself to the true tzadikim, from whom one receives the souls and the holy breaths, as above. For all the souls of Israel need to receive the power of the holy breaths from the tzadikim of the generation, as above. And this is the aspect of t&rsquo;kiah, from the language of &ldquo;striking the hand&rdquo; [t&rsquo;kias kaf], which means binding together. As it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;All the nations, clap your hands&rdquo;</span> [kol ha&rsquo;amim tik&rsquo;u chaf] <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 47:2)</span> &mdash; which Rashi explained as: &ldquo;join together&rdquo; &mdash; that is, they should intermingle and bind together to sound a blast to G&ndash;d, etc.</p>

<p><em>Sh&rsquo;varim</em> &mdash; this is the aspect of a broken and crushed heart [laiv nishbar v&rsquo;nidkeh] &mdash; the aspect of longing and powerful yearnings for Hashem, blessed be He, through which one&rsquo;s heart is constantly broken because of the greatness of the yearnings and the longing with which one yearns with a powerful will for Hashem, blessed be He.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>t&rsquo;ruah</em> &mdash; an expression of love and longing for Hashem, blessed be He, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;He has not beheld iniquity in Yaakov, etc., and the t&rsquo;ruas melech [the friendship/love of the King] is in him&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bamidbar 23:21)</span>. And Rashi explained: an expression of affection and friendship &mdash; that is, the aspect of love and will, the aspect of love and longing for Hashem, blessed be He, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;For I am lovesick&rdquo;</span> [ki cholas ahavah ani] <span class="inline-source">(Shir HaShirim 2:5)</span>, as is brought in the Torah teaching mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <em>final t&rsquo;kiah</em> &mdash; to go back and bind the entire world to the yearnings and the souls and the holy breaths, in order to bring them all back to good. In the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it shall be on that day, a great shofar shall be blown, and the lost shall come, etc., and the scattered,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 27:13)</span>. For the first t&rsquo;kiah is to bind ourselves to the true tzadikim, in order to receive from them the breaths and the holy souls, as above. And the final t&rsquo;kiah is in order to bind to us also the entire world &mdash; that they should all receive these breaths and holy souls, so that they should all return to Hashem, blessed be He, through this, and accept the yoke of His sovereignty upon themselves &mdash; in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;All the nations, clap your hands,&rdquo;</span> etc.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;12</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchuyos, Zichronos, and Shofaros</span> [Sovereignty, Remembrances, and Shofar Blasts] that we say in the prayer on Rosh HaShanah.</p>

<p>For it is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above that one must express the holy yearnings with one&rsquo;s mouth, so that the soul should come forth from potential to actual. And for this the order of the prayers was instituted &mdash; see there. And this is the aspect of Malchuyos, etc. &mdash; that we express the holy yearnings with our mouths. For Malchuyos is that we accept the yoke of His sovereignty upon ourselves, and we pray that His sovereignty should be revealed over the entire world &mdash; which is the essential holy yearnings: that one must constantly yearn and long to accept the yoke of His sovereignty upon oneself with love, and to express these yearnings with one&rsquo;s mouth, as above. And then these breaths have the power to go and arouse the entire world to teshuvah &mdash; and this is the aspect of the blowing of the shofar, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>Zichronos</em> [Remembrances] &mdash; for then we pray that He should remember for us His covenant that He established with our fathers. And we mention all the verses that speak of this, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And G&ndash;d heard their groaning, and G&ndash;d remembered His covenant with them,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Shemos 2:24)</span>. And it says:</p>

<p><span class="verse">&ldquo;And I will remember My covenant with Yaakov,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Vayikra 26:42)</span>. And we conclude: &ldquo;And the Akeidah of Yitzchak for his seed, etc., may You remember. Blessed, etc., Who remembers the covenant.&rdquo; That is, we now pray that He should draw upon us the merit of the guarding of the bris of our fathers, the tzadikim &mdash; in order that through this, the havalim [breaths] of the Sitra Achara, which are made from evil yearnings, should have no power to confuse the world, to cause sin, G&ndash;d forbid, through their evil vanities, in the aspect of: &ldquo;There is a hevel,&rdquo; etc., as above. For the merit of the tikun habris of our fathers will overpower and ascend before Him, blessed be He, until through this all the holy breaths of the holy yearnings of Israel will be sifted and elevated. And all the breaths of the Sitra Achara &mdash; of the evil yearnings &mdash; will be nullified before them as nothing and naught.</p>

<p>And therefore the verses of Zichronos begin with the matter of Noach, as we say: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And also Noach, with love You remembered,&rdquo;</span> etc., as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And G&ndash;d remembered Noach, etc., and all that was with him in the teivah [ark]. And G&ndash;d caused a wind to pass over the earth, and the waters subsided&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 8:1)</span>.</p>

<p>For Hashem, blessed be He, commanded Noach to enter the teivah, to be enclosed there from before the waters of the Mabul [Flood] &mdash; even though there was much deliverance and salvation before Him. But the matter is well explained according to the above: because the generation had corrupted their deeds greatly, and went after their desires and their evil yearnings, until the world was full of evil breaths [havalim ra&rsquo;im] that are made from evil yearnings &mdash; until it was not possible for the world to endure. Therefore He brought upon them the waters of the Mabul.</p>

<p>And then Noach had to enter the teivah and be enclosed there &mdash; so that he would not receive and absorb the evil breaths of the world, of the evil yearnings. For this was the essential aspect of the <span class="key-term">ruach ra&rsquo;ah</span> [evil spirit] that ruled over the world then &mdash; that is, an actual evil spirit made from evil yearnings. Because of this he had to be enclosed in the teivah, in order to hide himself from the evil breaths that are the evil spirit made from evil yearnings &mdash; through which was the essential destruction of the world at that time. And as is explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above, that through evil yearnings, souls are made that are the aspect of vowel-points, and they give the letters an evil configuration, in the aspect of: &ldquo;If he does not merit, it becomes a potion of death for him&rdquo; [lo zachah na&rsquo;asais lo sam maves] &mdash; G&ndash;d protect us. And through this they destroyed the world at that time.</p>

<p>And Noach had to hide from them in the teivah so that the evil breaths should not have power over him, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the matter of what is brought in the Zohar: that in a time of distress [b&rsquo;idan ak&rsquo;sa] one must hide. That is, as above &mdash; the essential root of all the troubles, G&ndash;d protect us, is drawn from evil souls that are made from evil yearnings, through which the letters of the Torah are given a configuration in the reverse direction, G&ndash;d forbid, as above. And therefore one must hide in a room, so as not to absorb from the evil breaths, which are the aspect of an evil spirit, G&ndash;d protect us. And as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Go, My people, enter your chambers and close your door behind you; hide for a brief moment until the fury passes&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 26:20)</span>. For one must close oneself in one&rsquo;s room until the fury and wrath passes &mdash; which is made from evil breaths, as above.</p>

<p>And Hashem, blessed be He, in His mercy, then remembered Noach the tzaddik who was in the teivah &mdash; <span class="verse">&ldquo;and G&ndash;d caused a wind to pass over the earth.&rdquo;</span> And Rashi explained: a &ldquo;wind of comfort&rdquo; [ruach naicha], etc. That is, in His mercy He gave power so that the holy breaths of Noach and all who were with him in the teivah should overpower &mdash; and they are the aspect of a good spirit, a spirit of comfort. And through this, &ldquo;the waters subsided&rdquo; &mdash; and the waters of the Mabul were nullified, whose essential dominion was through the evil spirit of the evil yearnings, as above.</p>

<p>And for this we pray &mdash; that also now He should have mercy upon us and remember all the holy breaths of Israel, of the good yearnings, and sift them from the breaths of the Sitra Achara, of the evil yearnings, so that they should have no power to rule over them, to confuse the world, G&ndash;d forbid. Especially since now we have something to rely upon, for we have already had great and awesome tzadikim who guarded the bris to the utmost. And we ask that He should remember for us their merit &mdash; and this is the matter of all the verses of Zichronos that we say afterward: that He should remember for us the covenant of our fathers. And we conclude with the Akeidah of Yitzchak, etc.</p>

<p>For the Akeidah of Yitzchak is the essential aspect of good yearnings &mdash; that he sacrificed his soul with intense passion in truth, to do His will, blessed be He &mdash; from which is rooted the holy point in the heart of every one of Israel, to yearn and desire Hashem, blessed be He, with self-sacrifice, as above. And therefore we ask that He should remember all of this for us &mdash; so that the holy breaths should overpower through the power of the tzadikim who guarded the bris, and they should ascend before Him with favor, and they should have the power to bring the entire world back in teshuvah. And the evil breaths &mdash; which are the aspect of the waters of the Mabul &mdash; should have no power to rule over them, to confuse the world, G&ndash;d forbid.</p>

<p>And this is the essential aspect of <em>z&rsquo;chirah</em> [remembrance] &mdash; that we pray that He should remember for us the merit of our fathers and the Akeidah of Yitzchak, etc. That is, that the evil breaths should not confuse, G&ndash;d forbid. For certainly there is no forgetting before Him, blessed be He. But when, G&ndash;d forbid, the evil breaths overpower against the good breaths &mdash; this is the aspect of forgetting, which is the aspect of &ldquo;clouds that cover over the eyes&rdquo; [ananan dim&rsquo;chas&rsquo;yan al ainyin] &mdash; that is, the good is not recognizable, G&ndash;d forbid, because the evil covers over it, G&ndash;d forbid. But we come with the power of our fathers who guarded the bris to the utmost. And we remind Him, blessed be He, that even in the generation of the Mabul &mdash; when the entire generation was evil, and there was only Noach, a lone individual in the world, and there was not then the merit of holy tzadikim such as these &mdash; even so, Hashem, blessed be He, had mercy and remembered Noach, and caused the holy breaths to overpower the waters of the Mabul.</p>

<p>And how much more so now, when Israel in general &mdash; the majority of them, virtually all of them &mdash; yearn very, very much for Hashem, blessed be He, with great yearnings and self-sacrifice. And we have already had holy tzadikim such as these, from the days of our fathers until now &mdash; through whose merit it is certainly fitting that all the evil breaths in the world should be nullified and become as nothing and naught, and the holy breaths of the good yearnings should overpower and strengthen, until they bring the entire world back in teshuvah. And this is the entire matter of Rosh HaShanah, which is the first of the Ten Days of Teshuvah, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of <em>Shofaros</em>. For afterward we pray that the holy breaths should go forth and arouse also the entire world in teshuvah &mdash; and this is the aspect of the verses of Shofaros. For this is the essential aspect of the receiving of the Torah through the sound of the shofar. For Moshe Rabbainu, in the immensity of his power, drew the power of the holy breaths, which are the aspect of holy souls &mdash; through which the letters of the Torah were given a good configuration. And through this he merited to give the Torah then.</p>

<p>For in truth, the Torah already existed even before that, for the Torah preceded the world. However, the letters of the Torah have no configuration and no effect except according to the vowel-points that are made through the yearnings, etc. &mdash; as is well explained in the Torah teaching mentioned above, see there. And therefore the Torah was not given until Moshe came. For then Israel was purified through the power of Moshe, until their holy yearnings overpowered and gave the letters of the Torah a good configuration. And therefore the Torah was given with the sound of the shofar, which is the aspect of the holy breaths, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And the sound of the shofar was very strong,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Shemos 19:16)</span>. &ldquo;Very strong&rdquo; specifically &mdash; that is, the sound of the shofar, which is the holy breaths, was going and getting very strong, in order to subdue and break all the breaths of the Sitra Achara, so that they should have no power to give the letters of the Torah a configuration in the reverse direction, G&ndash;d forbid, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore after the verses of Shofaros we pray that He should gather all the scattered ones, as it is written: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And it shall be on that day, a great shofar shall be blown, and the lost shall come, and the scattered,&rdquo;</span> etc. <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 27:13)</span>. For this is the essential blessing of Shofaros &mdash; that the holy breaths of the shofar should overpower, and go and spread throughout the world, until they bring the entire world back in teshuvah, and all the scattered and the lost should be gathered, to bring them all back to holiness. And everything is through the power of the holy breaths, as above.</p>

